To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Illinois Freedom of Information Act., I hereby request the following records:

This request is intended to specifically identify existing records and is not a request for the Village to create, compile, analyze, or answer questions.

Subject: Christopher B. Burke Engineering, Ltd. (“CBBEL”) – September 2021 Stormwater Engineering Task Order #4

I am specifically seeking the CBBEL work products and supporting records relating to the portion of the September 2021 Task Order concerning “Immediate Projects for Depressional Areas,” as well as the related evaluation of stormwater storage/retention opportunities in open-space areas, potential property acquisitions/buyouts, underground storage, and other distributed flood-storage opportunities.

Please provide the following records created, received, or maintained by the Village from September 1, 2021 through December 31, 2022, including records subsequently received or maintained by the Village that document or transmit the results of this work:

1.  All final or completed CBBEL reports, memoranda, technical memoranda, studies, analyses, presentations, slide decks, exhibits, maps, drawings, tables, spreadsheets, calculations, site evaluations, conceptual plans, or other work products produced pursuant to Christopher B. Burke Engineering Task Order #4 concerning stormwater management.

2.  All records specifically concerning the identification or evaluation of open-space locations as potential locations for stormwater storage, detention, retention, flood storage, water retention, underground storage, or other flood-mitigation purposes.

This includes, without limitation, records containing:

- maps or lists of potential open-space storage locations;
- identification or evaluation of specific properties or sites;
- conceptual storage alternatives;
- estimated storage capacity or volume;
- acreage or site-area calculations;
- flood-volume calculations;
- conceptual grading or drainage information;
- evaluations of the feasibility of using open space for temporary or permanent stormwater storage;
- comparisons of alternative storage locations; and
- recommendations concerning whether particular locations should be studied further.

3.  All maps, exhibits, figures, GIS maps, aerial photographs, site plans, or other graphical materials prepared by or for CBBEL that depict or identify potential stormwater storage, flood-storage, detention, retention, or mitigation locations.

4.  All records evaluating or identifying property acquisition, property buyout, easement, or other property-control opportunities as a means of creating or expanding stormwater storage or flood-mitigation capacity, including any maps, property lists, site evaluations, cost estimates, or recommendations.

5.  All records concerning underground stormwater storage or storage beneath/within publicly owned or publicly accessible open-space areas, including evaluations of schools, parks, Park District property, Village property, the La Grange Country Club, or other open-space properties.

6.  All CBBEL presentations or presentation materials concerning the results of the September 2021 Task Order, including presentations made to or prepared for:
- the Village Board;
- Village staff;
- the Environmental Quality Commission;
- the Park District of La Grange;
- School District 105;
- School District 204; or
- any other governmental body or public meeting.

7.  All records transmitting, submitting, presenting, or distributing the above-described CBBEL work products, including transmittal memoranda, cover letters, staff reports, agenda attachments, presentation materials, or meeting materials.

8.  All records that specifically identify the “areas of potential future study” resulting from the September 2021 CBBEL stormwater analysis, including any maps, lists, memoranda, presentations, recommendations, or site evaluations identifying those areas.

9.  All records constituting or supporting the stormwater-related work product that resulted in, or was used to prepare, the FEMA BRIC application referenced by the Village as one of the results of the September 2021 CBBEL task order, but only to the extent those records concern the identification, evaluation, design, or analysis of potential stormwater-storage or flood-mitigation locations.

10.  All versions of the above records that were provided to the Village, including draft, preliminary, revised, and final versions, if maintained by the Village.
Specific date/context identifiers

For purposes of locating the records, this request concerns the Christopher B. Burke Engineering stormwater work associated with:

- the September 2021 Stormwater Engineering Task Order / Task Order #4;
- the Task Order component concerning “Immediate Projects for Depressional Areas”;
- stormwater storage opportunities in open space;
- property buyout opportunities;
- underground stormwater storage;
- flood-mitigation opportunities involving schools, parks, open space, or other properties; and
- the CBBEL work that the Village subsequently described as identifying “areas of potential future study.”

The Village has publicly stated that in September 2021 it entered into a CBBEL task order covering four additional stormwater engineering areas, including “immediate projects for depressional areas,” and that the results included identification of areas for potential future study. The Village also stated that these projects were generally anticipated to be completed by the end of 2021.

The Village Board meeting records from this period also refer to CBBEL stormwater engineering work involving potential flood-mitigation options and stormwater storage opportunities.

Electronic production

Please provide the responsive records electronically in their existing electronic format, preferably by email or electronic download.

For maps, drawings, presentations, spreadsheets, GIS materials, or other records that are maintained electronically, please provide the original electronic format where reasonably available rather than a printed/scanned reproduction.

If any responsive record contains exempt material, please redact only the exempt portion and provide the remainder of the record pursuant to FOIA's severability requirement.

If the Village believes any portion of this request is unduly burdensome or requires clarification, please contact me before denying the request so that the request may be narrowed to manageable proportions.

Thank you.

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 5 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Concerned Citizen of La Grange
